---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
---

<Layout title="About — SCaLE Trip" description="About this SCaLE 24x trip planner.">
  <Nav />
  <main>
    <div class="about-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="section-label">About This Site</p>
        <h1>SCaLE 24x 2027</h1>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="container">
      <div class="about-grid">
        <section class="card about-card">
          <h2>The Trip</h2>
          <p>
            A solo trip to Pasadena, California for <a href="https://www.socallinuxexpo.org/scale/24x" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SCaLE 24x</a>,
            the Southern California Linux Expo.
          </p>
          <ul class="about-list">
            <li>✈️ Flying SEA → LAX/BUR from Seattle-Tacoma</li>
            <li>📅 April 1–4, 2027 (4 days)</li>
            <li>🐧 SCaLE 24x: Apr 1–4</li>
            <li>🌴 Solo traveler</li>
            <li>🍦 Ice cream selfie tradition (4 spots planned)</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="card about-card">
          <h2>The Site</h2>
          <p>
            This is a personal trip planner built with <a href="https://astro.build" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Astro</a>
            and hosted on <a href="https://pages.github.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub Pages</a>.
            It's part of a monorepo of trip planners at <a href="/" >sfalken.github.io</a>.
          </p>
          <ul class="about-list">
            <li>🗺️ Interactive maps (Leaflet + OpenStreetMap)</li>
            <li>✅ Planning checklist with browser persistence</li>
            <li>💰 Budget tracker with expense logging</li>
            <li>📱 Progressive Web App (installable, offline-capable)</li>
            <li>🔒 Optional PII encryption for booking details</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="card about-card">
          <h2>SCaLE 24x</h2>
          <p>
            SCaLE is the Southern California Linux Expo, the largest community-run open source and
            free software conference in North America. It brings together users, developers, and companies
            for talks, workshops, an expo hall, and co-located events.
          </p>
          <p style="margin-top:.75rem;">
            Held at the Pasadena Convention Center, 300 E Green St. Registration pricing and the full schedule
            had not been published when this site was built.
          </p>
          <a href="https://www.socallinuxexpo.org/scale/24x" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-primary" style="margin-top:1rem;align-self:flex-start;">
            Visit socallinuxexpo.org →
          </a>
        </section>

        <section class="card about-card">
          <h2>Pasadena, California</h2>
          <p>
            Pasadena sits just northeast of downtown Los Angeles, known for the Rose Bowl, the Rose Parade,
            Caltech, and the walkable Old Pasadena dining district.
          </p>
          <ul class="about-list">
            <li>🕐 Timezone: Pacific Time (same as Seattle)</li>
            <li>🚆 Metro L (Gold) Line: Memorial Park station, a half-mile walk from the venue</li>
            <li>✈️ Airports: Burbank (BUR) is closest; LAX has more flights</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about-hero {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--ca-primary) 0%, var(--ca-accent) 100%);
    color: white;
    padding: 2.5rem 0 2rem;
  }
  .about-hero .section-label { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.7); }
  .about-hero h1 { color: white; }

  .about-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(300px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .about-card {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }
  .about-card h2 { font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--ca-primary); }
  .about-card p { font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--gray-700); line-height: 1.6; }

  .about-list {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--gray-700);
  }
</style>
